This patch is applied to the pinned services.jar smali during the existing
M1E framework overlay build.

The rootless runtime cannot create timerfd CLOCK_*_ALARM descriptors and uses
AlarmManagerService.AlarmHandler.ALARM_EVENT. The pinned fallback directly
calls PendingIntent.isActivity() and PendingIntent.send() for every due Alarm.
Listener alarms are valid and represent their target with alarm.listener while
alarm.operation is null. AlarmManager's internal TIME_TICK trigger is such a
listener and is scheduled for each minute boundary. Android's regular alarm path calls
deliverAlarmsLocked(), which routes both PendingIntent and listener alarms
through DeliveryTracker and updates alarm bookkeeping.

The overlay changes only the fallback dispatch: while holding the existing
mLock, it calls deliverAlarmsLocked(triggerList, nowElapsed), reschedules the
next alarm, and updates alarm-clock state. This preserves listener callback,
completion, wake-lock, and alarm-count handling. The stock framework image and
original services.jar remain immutable.

Reference implementation:
https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/a38d32bb09756370c5c28d210a051415e85e0be2/apex/jobscheduler/service/java/com/android/server/alarm/AlarmManagerService.java
